[Music]  back in the 1960s Italian architect  Paolo Soleri believed that the urban  planning of his time  was not sustainable he believed the  cities were too big too wasteful into  isolating his dream was to build a  harmonious town that would balance  architecture and ecology he thought this  is how people are meant to live simple  social sustainable are here the locals  are known as arcanas and this side is  our urban laboratory so where he called  his philosophy our ecology and he wanted  to prove that it was more than just a  utopian vision he wanted to make it real  so Larry was once a student of the  legendary American architect Frank Lloyd  Wright and like right he had the  students construct his visionary  buildings by hand what they learned his  philosophy and methodology salera lived  nearby in Paradise Valley Arizona his  home in studio called Kazan T is now  surrounded by golf courses and  McMansions however it remains a  brilliant example of organic  architecture today the subterranean  buildings and winding paths are open to  the public and you can see they seem  ahead every time  at arc Asante most of the structures are  built using a method called silk casting  dirt pulled from the site is used to  create forms which are then filled with  concrete  once the concrete sets the forms were  broken and brushed away with the dirt  returning to the earth walkways bridges  and stairs connect the structures  natural solar energy is used for warmth  in winter while don't sand canopies  cooling summer there are spaces for  living working and entertaining just  feet away from each other since 1970  over 7,000 people have lived and worked  at Arcosanti right now about 80 people  live here from all corners of the globe  since the early days arc Asante has been  funded by the sale of polish Larry's  famous wind bells these bells are cast  by hand in this foundry  [Music]  no new buildings have been dedicated  since 1989  and so Larry passed away in 2013 but  Arcosanti is still a laboratory where  city living  is explored plus the foundation now has  a couple of rooms available on Airbnb  and a music festival called forum  Arcosanti is held here in the spring  this community was intended to be a  prototype so Larry thought that there  will be many ARCA scientists at each new  version would be an improvement one has  to accept the notion of failure he said  the next step will be more promising  than the last  [Music]

